        },
        "texto": "See also Matthew 7:24. In building the better class of houses it is usual to dig down until the solid rock is reached, in order to have a sure foundation for the edifice. Dr. Robinson says of a new house he visited in Nazareth, by invitation of its owner, “In order to lay the fou…"
      },
      "c-f87a0fff516c4d92": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-760",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The term “bosom” frequently refers, in Oriental usage, to the folds of the garment as they extend beyond and droop over the girdle. This part of the dress is also called the “lap.”‘ See 2 Kings 4:39 and see also note on Neh. 5:13 (#380). It is used as a receptacle for various art…"
      }
